From: robertijtsma <37256770+robertijtsma@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] media: qcom: camss: full SC8180X / Titan 175 bring-up with VFE Lite, FIFO, privacy LEDs and RDI fixes

Complete working qcom-camss patch against Linux v7.3 for Qualcomm SC8180X
(Microsoft Surface Pro X SQ2), cleaned and verified against spx/v7.3
(upstream PR linux-surface/kernel#206) without disturbing any other SoC:

- External generic PHY CSIPHY subdev integration (including camss-csiphy.h)
  preserving legacy built-in CSIPHYs untouched for all other SoCs.
- VFE-17x / VFE-Lite fixes: STATUS_1_RDI_SOF checked on status1,
  !vfe_is_lite() guard on VFE_BUS_WM_DEBUG_STATUS_CFG (0x226c), valid
  Lite reset bitmask and 4-client WM_ADDR_NO_SYNC_LITE_VAL (0xf),
  2-deep VFE_BUS_WM_IMAGE_ADDR FIFO with coherent VFE_DUMMY_BUF underrun
  fallback, single WM_CLIENT_BUF_DONE IRQ subscription, VFE_CORE_CFG = 0,
  vfe_halt(), IRQF_NO_AUTOEN, and lock-safe vfe_flush_buffers().
- CSID gen2 fixes: unpacked 16-bit plain LSB RAW10 formats
  (Y10_2X8_PADHI_LE / SBGGR10_2X8_PADHI_LE), csid_reset_retain_sw_reg(),
  proper RDI_CFG0_ENABLE clearing on stop, and parent_dev_ops error unwind.
- SC8180X / SM8150 resource tables (400 MHz vfe*_cphy_rx, camnoc_dcd_xo,
  vfe0/1_dsp) with CAMSS_8150-scoped NoC-safe power/clock retention and
  warm vfe_reset() on reuse.
- Optional DT privacy LED GPIOs (privacy-led-front/rear-gpios), pipeline
  rollback, sink-to-source teardown, and RDI __video_try_fmt() clamping.

Note: Supersedes Patch 0003 when applying onto vanilla Linux v7.3
(requires phy-qcom-mipi-csi2 and camcc-sc8180x).

Base: Linux v7.3 (spx/v7.3)

Signed-off-by: robertijtsma <37256770+robertijtsma@users.noreply.github.com>
